      style 21 fill:#d4e8fc,stroke:#94a2b0,color:#000000
      22("<div style='font-weight: bold'>src.wrapKeyBundle</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: function]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Encrypt a keypair bundle with<br />a wrapping key. The wrapping<br />key is used as IKM for HKDF —<br />it must be at least 32 bytes.<br />Typically derived from a user<br />passphrase (Argon2id/scrypt)<br />or from another key exchange.<br />Do not use a low-entropy<br />string directly. Returns a<br />JSON-serialisable object —<br />all byte fields are base64url<br />strings.</div>")
      style 22 fill:#d4e8fc,stroke:#94a2b0,color:#000000
      23("<div style='font-weight: bold'>src.unwrapKeyBundle</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: function]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Decrypt a keypair bundle<br />produced by wrapKeyBundle().<br />Verifies the HMAC-SHA512 MAC<br />in constant time before<br />attempting decryption. Throws<br />on MAC failure, wrong key, or<br />any corrupt data — never<br />returns a partially recovered<br />keypair.</div>")
      style 23 fill:#d4e8fc,stroke:#94a2b0,color:#000000
      24("<div style='font-weight: bold'>src.openMemoryStore</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: function]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>In-memory KeyStore backed by<br />a Map. Stores the opaque<br />ChannelKeypairs handle<br />directly — no serialization<br />overhead. Use in Node.js,<br />Cloudflare Workers, and<br />tests. Data does not persist<br />across process restarts.</div>")
      style 24 fill:#d4e8fc,stroke:#94a2b0,color:#000000
      25("<div style='font-weight: bold'>src.openIndexedDBStore</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: function]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>IndexedDB-backed KeyStore.<br />Serializes keypairs to<br />4,800-byte ArrayBuffers and<br />stores them in an IndexedDB<br />object store. Data persists<br />across page reloads. Uses<br />lazy connection<br />initialisation — the DB is<br />opened on first use and the<br />connection is reused for<br />subsequent operations. Object<br />store name: 'keypairs' DB<br />version: 1</div>")
      style 25 fill:#d4e8fc,stroke:#94a2b0,color:#000000
      26("<div style='font-weight: bold'>src.openKeyStore</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: function]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Open the best available<br />KeyStore for the current<br />environment. Returns an<br />IndexedDB store if<br />`indexedDB` is available<br />(browsers), or a memory store<br />(Node.js, Cloudflare<br />Workers).</div>")
      style 26 fill:#d4e8fc,stroke:#94a2b0,color:#000000
      27("<div style='font-weight: bold'>src.toArrayBuffer</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: function]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Convert a Uint8Array to a<br />plain ArrayBuffer. Web Crypto<br />requires ArrayBuffer (not<br />ArrayBufferLike) for all key<br />and data parameters. Noble<br />functions return<br />Uint8Array<ArrayBufferLike>,<br />which may be backed by a<br />SharedArrayBuffer. This<br />ensures we always pass a<br />plain ArrayBuffer to satisfy<br />both the DOM types and<br />runtime requirements.</div>")
      style 27 fill:#d4e8fc,stroke:#94a2b0,color:#000000
      28("<div style='font-weight: bold'>src.importAesKey</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: function]</div>")
      style 28 fill:#d4e8fc,stroke:#94a2b0,color:#000000
      29("<div style='font-weight: bold'>src.aesGcmEncrypt</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: function]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>AES-256-GCM encrypt. Returns<br />ciphertext with the 16-byte<br />GCM auth tag appended. The<br />caller is responsible for<br />generating a unique 12-byte<br />IV per encryption. Reusing an<br />IV with the same key is<br />catastrophic — this function<br />does not enforce uniqueness;<br />callers must generate IVs via<br />randomIv().</div>")
      style 29 fill:#d4e8fc,stroke:#94a2b0,color:#000000
      30("<div style='font-weight: bold'>src.aesGcmDecrypt</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: function]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>AES-256-GCM decrypt. Throws<br />if the GCM auth tag is<br />invalid. This is a secondary<br />authentication check; callers<br />should validate the outer<br />HMAC-SHA512 MAC before<br />calling this.</div>")
      style 30 fill:#d4e8fc,stroke:#94a2b0,color:#000000
      31("<div style='font-weight: bold'>src.hmacSha512</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: function]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Compute HMAC-SHA512. Used as<br />the outer MAC in<br />Encrypt-then-MAC. The message<br />should include both the nonce<br />and the ciphertext to prevent<br />nonce-swapping attacks.</div>")
      style 31 fill:#d4e8fc,stroke:#94a2b0,color:#000000
      32("<div style='font-weight: bold'>src.constantTimeEqual</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: function]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Constant-time byte equality<br />check. Always use this — not<br />===, not a manual loop — when<br />comparing MACs or secrets.<br />Timing-safe comparison<br />prevents MAC oracle attacks.</div>")
      style 32 fill:#d4e8fc,stroke:#94a2b0,color:#000000
